## §3 Generating Android-ready graphics **[core]**

### Play Store asset spec

| Asset | Size | Format | Rules |
|-------|------|--------|-------|
| **App icon (listing)** | **512×512** | **32-bit PNG ONLY** | **CRITICAL: No JPEGs.** Must include alpha channel. Flat 2D graphic only (no device photos). Keep core art inside a **15% padding safe zone** to account for Google's automatic 30% squircle mask. |
| **Feature graphic** | **1024×500** | PNG/JPEG | Exact dimensions required (1023x500 will fail). No transparency. No misleading text (“#1”, “Free money”). |
| **Phone screenshots** | min 2; long side **1080+** | PNG/JPEG | **9:16** or **16:9**. Must depict **real in-app UI**. |
| **Adaptive launcher** | foreground **432×432** | PNG in `mipmap-*` | Must visually match the 512x512 Store Icon to prevent Misleading Claims policy violations. |

### Launcher icon — density table

Generate from one **1024×1024** master (keep safe zone ~66% center for adaptive crop):

| Folder | px |
|--------|-----|
| `mipmap-mdpi` | 48 |
| `mipmap-hdpi` | 72 |
| `mipmap-xhdpi` | 96 |
| `mipmap-xxhdpi` | 144 |
| `mipmap-xxxhdpi` | 192 |

**Adaptive icon:** `mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml` — separate **background color** (`values/colors.xml`) and **foreground** PNG. Match Balance default: background `#0A0A0A`, foreground = brand mark (e.g. gold cairn / 3×3 grid motif).

### How we generate images (workflow)

1. **Design brief** — one sentence: subject, background color, flat vs gradient, **no text** on launcher icon unless it exists in-app.
2. **Master art** — Cursor **GenerateImage** or Figma export at 1024×1024 (icon) and 1024×500 (feature graphic). Prefer **simple geometric marks** (Equalize: stacked stones / 3×3 grid) over busy screenshots for the icon.
3. **Resize / density export**
   - **Play listing icon:** Export **512×512 32-bit PNG** with alpha — verify with `file play-store-icon-512.png` (must say "PNG image data, 512 x 512, 8-bit/color RGBA"). **Never upload JPEG.**
   - **Android Studio:** Right-click `res` → **New → Image Asset** → Launcher Icons (Adaptive and Legacy) → import master PNG.
   - **CLI (macOS):** `sips -z 512 512 master.png --out play-store-icon-512.png`; loop sizes for mipmaps.
   - **ImageMagick:** `magick master.png -resize 144x144 mipmap-xxhdpi/ic_launcher.png`
4. **Store screenshots** — Playwright or emulator:
   ```bash
   npx playwright screenshot --viewport-size=390,844 \
     "file:///path/to/game.html" screenshot-tutorial.png
   ```
   Capture: tutorial, mid-game, win state. Run at **390×844** (embed) and **1080×2400** (Play upload) by scaling or device frame.
5. **Sanity check** — Side-by-side: **launcher icon ↔ first screen ↔ Play listing icon**. Google **Misleading Claims** rejections often come from icons/screenshots that promise UI the app does not show (wrong colors, fake “Level 100”, DSA/LeetCode logos on a puzzle game, etc.).

### Play Store listing honesty checklist

- Icon = what users see after install (same palette and motif).
- Screenshots = **Balance theme** (or documented default), not one-off marketing mocks.
- Short/full description matches **actual** features (no “500 levels” if 35, no “online multiplayer” if local-only).
- Feature graphic: game name + real board art; avoid stock “brain training” clip art unrelated to the product.

