## §4 Build & sync pipeline **[core]**

### Capacitor (full site)

```bash
# From web repo root — NOT android/
npm run build
npx cap copy android          # assets only
# npx cap sync android        # after new Capacitor plugins / native config
```

Open `android/` in Android Studio → Run.

### WebView shell (single HTML game)

1. Edit web game in **parent repo** (`equalize.html`, `levels.js`, …).
2. Gradle `syncEqualizeWebAssets` (or equivalent) runs before `merge*Assets` — copies into `app/build/generated/equalizeAssetsDebug|Release`.
3. **Debug** keeps test hooks; **Release** strips debug globals.
4. Increment **`versionCode`** (integer, always up) and **`versionName`** (user string) in `app/build.gradle(.kts)` before every Play upload.

### Version bump discipline

| Field | Rule |
|-------|------|
| `versionCode` | +1 every Play Console upload |
| `versionName` | Semver string users see (e.g. `2.0.2`) |
| Web + Android | Bump Android when **web assets** shipped to Play change materially (tutorial, levels, themes) |

